      "id": "final-sale-damaged-exception",
      "category": "multi-source-grounding",
      "passed": false,
      "error": "",
      "agent_errors": [],
      "final_answer": "A broken zipper is a defect that can be handled even if the item is marked **FINAL\u202fSALE**.  \nAccording to our policy, final\u2011sale only stops returns for a change of mind, not for items that arrive damaged or defective. You can still have the item inspected and receive a resolution (replacement, refund, or other appropriate action). Since the bag arrived just yesterday, you\u2019re well within the reporting window of 7\u202fcalendar days.  \n\nHere\u2019s what to do next:\n\n1. **Gather evidence** \u2013 Take clear photos of the broken zipper and of the original packaging (if you still have it).  \n2. **Send a quick report** \u2013 In the chat, provide your order ID (if you have it) along with the photos and a short description of the defect.  \n3. **No return\u2011shipping fee** \u2013 Because the item is reported as damaged, the $6.95 return\u2011shipping fee is waived (or we can arrange free return shipping).  \n4. **Resolution options** \u2013 We\u2019ll review the photos. If the defect is confirmed, we can offer you a replacement bag or a refund, depending on availability and your preference.  \n5. **Warranty consideration** \u2013 Bags are covered by a 2\u2011year limited warranty against manufacturing defects, so you may also qualify for a warranty claim if the defect is proven to be a manufacturing issue.  \n\nOnce we receive your report, a human support specialist will review it and guide you through the next steps. Feel free to send the order ID and photos whenever you\u2019re ready.\n\n---",
